<h2 class="bde-heading-2244-121 bde-heading">
Founded and Edited by Dan Sweeting
</h2><p class="bde-f-text-2244-122 bde-f-text">
Dan started NBA Salaries in 2026 and runs it in his spare time. He decides what each page covers, which sources a figure can come from, and when a page needs updating.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-2244-123 bde-f-text">
He also runs F1 Salaries, a sister site on Formula 1 pay. Most NBA contracts are public, so the job here is different: keeping every player page and all 30 team payrolls accurate as trades, waivers, extensions and option decisions land through the season.
</p>
</div><div id="coverage" class="bde-fancy-container-2244-107 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-2244-124 bde-heading">
How the Site Works
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-125 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-135 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-143 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2244-158 bde-f-text">
Sources
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2244-144 bde-heading">
Public Records Only
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-145 bde-f-text">
Contract terms come from team announcements, the NBA's transaction log and established trackers such as Basketball-Reference and Hoops Rumors. Nothing comes from private documents.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-136 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-146 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2244-159 bde-f-text">
Checks
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2244-147 bde-heading">
Totals That Add Up
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-148 bde-f-text">
Team payrolls are rebuilt from each player's contract, so a team page, its roster table and every player page show the same figure.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-137 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-149 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2244-160 bde-f-text">
Updates
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2244-150 bde-heading">
Moves Logged as They Happen
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-151 bde-f-text">
When a player is traded, waived or extended, his page, both team pages and any teammate page that quotes the old payroll are updated together.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div><div id="standards" class="bde-fancy-container-2244-108 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-2244-126 bde-heading">
Independent and Free to Read
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-127 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-138 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2244-152 bde-heading">
No Ties to the League
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-153 bde-f-text">
NBA Salaries is not affiliated with the NBA, the NBPA, any team, agency or sportsbook, and no one can pay to change a figure.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-139 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2244-154 bde-heading">
Free for Everyone
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-155 bde-f-text">
There is no paywall and no sponsored content. If advertising is added, advertisers will have no say over what is published.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-140 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2244-156 bde-heading">
Corrections Welcome
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2244-157 bde-f-text">
If a figure looks wrong, send the page and a source. Every correction is checked and the page is updated.
</p>
</div>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2244-128 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



