<Fragment slot="body-19">
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/who-runs-nba-salaries/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/who-runs-nba-salaries/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why did you start NBA Salaries?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"NBA salary data is spread across trackers, team announcements and news reports, and most sites show a number without saying what it means. NBA Salaries puts each contract in context: how it compares with the team's payroll, the salary cap and the rest of the league."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you have inside access to NBA contracts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Every figure comes from public reporting and official announcements. NBA salaries are widely reported, but details such as guarantees and options sometimes differ between sources, and the site says so when they do."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How quickly are trades and signings added?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Moves are checked against more than one source before any page changes, so an update can take a few days after a deal is first reported."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is NBA Salaries connected to F1 Salaries?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Both sites are run by Dan Sweeting and follow the same approach: public sources, clear labels and figures that add up."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I report a mistake or suggest a page?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the contact form and include the page, the season and a link to your source."}}]}</script>
